( element_normal, manual Professional 6.445, 3D distorted mesh.
  2x2x2 hex8 mesh with non-planar faces. Rule (measured on the
  Professional): a node normal is the normalized sum over the boundary
  faces of the node of the consistent face normal integral( N_node n dA )
  (bilinear face, exact Gauss integration); the element_normal is the
  normalized sum of the node normals of the element nodes. Every element
  is a corner element. The targets are the Pro 02-08-2026 values (the
  consistent weighting matters: a plain face-area weighting differs by
  up to 8.e-3). Before the 2026-09-30 fix the GNU used the cross product
  of two edges of the first element face. )

